# Soccer Prediction Engine backend .env - copy to .env. The site works with NO keys at all (openfootball,
# football-data.co.uk, StatsBomb, and the international results/goalscorers CSVs are all
# free and keyless). Every variable below unlocks something extra and is optional.

# Path to the SQLite database. Optional - defaults to data/kickcast.db.
# KICKCAST_DB_PATH=data/kickcast.db

# football-data.org free tier (free, no cost, 10 req/min - real header-driven throttle
# in kickcast_api/football_data_org.py). VERIFIED WORKING with a real key: unlocks real
# Champions League fixtures/results (scripts/ingest.py's ingest_champions_league(), 144
# real 2026-27 league-phase matches fetched live on every ingest run - not a stale
# cache, since results change match to match and this tier has no daily cap). Does NOT
# unlock Champions League trophy odds/predictions - that needs a real cross-league
# team-strength rating, a separate unvalidated research task (kickcast_api/predictions.py
# explicitly refuses to fit an unvalidated model for "CL", even with enough matches).
# FOOTBALL_DATA_ORG_API_KEY=

# Gemini API free tier (free, no cost). Unlocks natural-language understanding for the
# "Ask about soccer" assistant: DB-first tool calls, then Wikipedia (see below) for
# facts outside our database. Without this, the assistant runs in a DB-only mode: a
# small set of keyword-matched question shapes, never natural language understanding.
# VERIFIED WORKING with a real key, but with 2 real, important findings:
#   1. The free tier's REAL daily cap for gemini-3.6-flash is 20 requests/day/project/
#      model (confirmed via a real 429: "GenerateRequestsPerDayPerProjectPerModel-
#      FreeTier... quotaValue: 20") - GEMINI_DAILY_QUOTA below defaults to this real
#      number now, not a guess.
#   2. Google Search grounding is NOT available on this tier for gemini-3.6-flash
#      (real 429 on the very first attempt, confirmed against Google's own pricing
#      docs - not a bug). The code path for it is still there and will activate
#      automatically if a future key/plan gets grounding access, but right now the
#      assistant's real "outside our DB" source is Wikipedia instead (free, keyless,
#      always available - see kickcast_api/assistant/wikipedia.py).
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Daily call budget before the assistant falls back to DB-only mode. Optional -
# defaults to 20 (the REAL free-tier cap - see above; don't raise this without a paid
# plan or a new real 429 confirming a higher number).
# GEMINI_DAILY_QUOTA=20

# Whether a plain DB lookup (next match, last result, table position, head-to-head
# prediction) is phrased by Gemini into a natural sentence (plus a brief, genuinely
# grounded extra like the opponent's form) instead of a fixed template sentence.
# Optional - defaults to true. Gemini is only ever given the facts we already looked up
# (never asked to invent one), and the result is cached by question+facts so a repeat
# question never costs quota again. Set to false to save quota if it's running tight -
# lookups still work, just as a plain template sentence instead ("mode": "db" in the
# response, with a note that AI phrasing is paused, if a key IS configured but this is
# turned off or quota ran out).
# ASSISTANT_GEMINI_FOR_LOOKUPS=true

# YouTube Data API v3 free tier (free, no cost, 10,000 quota units/day; search.list costs
# 100 units, so ~90 searches/day by default; channels.list costs only 1 unit). Used ONLY
# to attach an official highlight video link to an answer already sourced from our
# database or Wikipedia - never as a source of facts itself. Without this, answers just
# have no video link attached. VERIFIED WORKING with a real key.
# YOUTUBE_API_KEY=
# YOUTUBE_DAILY_QUOTA=90
# JSON map of channel name -> real YouTube channel ID, ADDING TO (not replacing) the
# verified defaults already checked into kickcast_api/assistant/youtube.py (UEFA,
# Premier League, LaLiga, Serie A, Bundesliga, Ligue 1 - each resolved via a real
# channels.list?forHandle=... call and confirmed by checking the response actually
# matches that channel, 2026-09-23). Use this to add more (e.g. a national team or a
# specific club's channel) without a code change.
# YOUTUBE_OFFICIAL_CHANNELS={"Some Other Channel": "UCxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx"}

# API-Football free tier (free, no cost, 100 requests/day). Unlocks the live match
# center (near-live scores/events, polled every 3 min into our own DB, never fetched on
# page load) using a REAL, verified team-ID crosswalk (kickcast_engine/data/
# api_football_crosswalk.py, 96/98 big-5 teams auto-resolved, 2 real naming-quirk
# overrides) instead of best-effort name matching, and real domestic-league Golden Boot
# / likely-goalscorer data (kickcast_api/domestic_scorers.py, GET /awards and
# /matches/{id}/prediction for the big-5). VERIFIED WORKING with a real key, with 1
# important real finding: the free plan does NOT have access to the current season -
# "Free plans do not have access to this season, try from 2022 to 2024" - so the
# Golden Boot/scorer data is real but is the 2024-25 season (the most recent this plan
# allows), not the live 2026-27 season; that needs a paid plan. Without this key,
# /matches/{id}/live always reports unavailable (Historical Replay mode, StatsBomb,
# keyless, real data, is shown instead), the live poller falls back to best-effort team
# NAME matching, and Golden Boot/domestic scorer data is unavailable.
# API_FOOTBALL_KEY=
# API_FOOTBALL_DAILY_QUOTA=100

# ESPN public scoreboard (keyless, undocumented, no published terms): a second results/live-score
# source - fills in scores, scorers and cards when API-Football's 100/day quota is spent, and covers
# the Nations League, which football-data.org's free tier does not. On in development, OFF in
# production unless you set this to true (same stance as ENABLE_API_FOOTBALL).
# ENABLE_ESPN=true
